{:edb/db-before-t 875 :edb/db-after-t 876 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534188 50 #inst "2026-10-06T08:57:20.843Z" 13194139534188 true] [17592186096552 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281268 13194139534188 true] [17592186096552 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281275 13194139534188 true] [17592186096553 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281289 13194139534188 true] [17592186096554 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281282 13194139534188 true] [17592186097189 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534188 true] [17592186097189 1100 "What is $\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^{4}(x + 1)^{2}\\,dx$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?" 13194139534188 false] [17592186097189 1100 "What is ${\\int }_{2}^{4}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?" 13194139534188 true] [17592186097189 1145 "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}f({x}_{m})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{m}=a+mΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{4}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=(x+1)^{2},$ the lower bound is $a=2$ and the upper bound is $b=4.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-2}{n}=\\frac{2}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}f({x}_{m})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[f(2+m\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[f(2+\\frac{2m}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[{((2+\\frac{2m}{n})+1)}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{m=1}^{n}[{(3+\\frac{2m}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534188 true] [17592186281268 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281269 13194139534188 true] [17592186281268 1089 "q-113880" 13194139534188 true] [17592186281268 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534188 true] [17592186281268 1100 "What is ${\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" 13194139534188 true] [17592186281268 1113 #uuid "a0fbe66e-c44a-5c47-b716-80288ecee20d" 13194139534188 true] [17592186281268 1145 "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)={e}^{x},$ the lower bound is $a=0,$ and the upper bound is $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-0}{n}=\\frac{3}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(0+i\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\,\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(\\frac{3i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{3i/n}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534188 true] [17592186281269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281270 13194139534188 true] [17592186281269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281271 13194139534188 true] [17592186281269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281272 13194139534188 true] [17592186281269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281273 13194139534188 true] [17592186281269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281274 13194139534188 true] [17592186281269 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534188 true] [17592186281269 1041 "selection" 13194139534188 true] [17592186281269 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281271 13194139534188 true] [17592186281269 1110 #uuid "1a2824ee-936d-5e13-b863-e43d4c60d600" 13194139534188 true] [17592186281270 1034 "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{3i/n}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3n}]" 13194139534188 true] [17592186281270 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534188 true] [17592186281270 1111 #uuid "a268cb6c-4f1f-528c-af25-723efe59